WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. On Thursday, July 19, 1990, Florida resident Steve McGowan received a letter in the mail from his 34-year-old sister, Beverly. The siblings had last spoken on Sunday, July 15, when Steve called Beverly to see if she would like to drop by for a visit.
我们的节目涉及严肃且往往令人痛心的事件。如果您在任何时候感到需要帮助，请联系当地的危机中心。如需获取保密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您使用的应用上或我们网站上的本集节目说明。1990年7月19日星期四，住在佛罗里达州的史蒂夫·麦高恩（Steve McGowan）收到了一封寄给他的信，寄信人是他34岁的妹妹贝弗利（Beverly）。兄妹俩最后一次通话是在7月15日星期日，当时史蒂夫打电话给贝弗利，问她愿不愿意过来串门。

2
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Beverly had declined, saying that she was too busy. Their conversation was pleasant and ordinary. Now, four days later, Steve was mildly surprised to find Beverly had sent him a letter out of the blue. The brief note contained the following message. I just want to say goodbye to you and the kids and let you know that what I am doing is the right thing. This is what I need at this point in my life, so don't worry.
贝弗利拒绝了，说她太忙了。他们的对话愉快而寻常。然而四天后，史蒂夫有些惊讶地发现贝弗利竟然无缘无故地给他写了一封信。这封简短的信里写着以下内容：我只想向你和孩子们道别，并让你知道我正在做的事情是正确的。这是我现阶段生活中所需要的，所以不用担心。

3
00:01:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
When I come back, I will be a much better and happier person. Beverly was the youngest of the three McGowan children. The family hailed from Philadelphia, but had all relocated to Florida a little over a decade earlier. Beverly lived on the coast in Pompano Beach. Her sister Jane lived 11 miles north in Boca Raton. Steve resided in central Florida. Like her brother, Jane also received a cryptic farewell letter from Beverly.
当我回来时，我会成为一个更好、更快乐的人。贝弗利是麦高恩家三个孩子中最小的一个。这家人原本来自费城，但在十多年前都搬到了佛罗里达州。贝弗利住在海岸边的庞帕诺比奇。她的姐姐简住在北面11英里外的博卡拉顿。史蒂夫则住在佛罗里达州中部。和她的哥哥一样，简也收到了贝弗利发来的神秘告别信。

4
00:02:28.000 --> 00:03:08.000
It detailed her decision to make some big life changes in order to go traveling. She wrote of quitting her job and selling her condo as she had to leave right away. The letters made little sense to Steve and Jane. After working hard for a long time, Beverly finally seemed happy with both her career and home life. She had recently purchased the condo and was working two jobs to pay off the mortgage. They couldn't understand why she would suddenly give up everything and leave without a proper goodbye.
信中详细说明了她为了去旅行而做出改变人生的重大决定的经过。她写道自己辞去了工作，卖掉了公寓，因为她必须马上离开。这封信对史蒂夫和简来说有些莫名其妙。在辛苦工作了很长时间后，贝弗利似乎终于对自己的职业和家庭生活感到满意了。她最近刚买下这套公寓，并打两份工来偿还房贷。他们无法理解她为什么会突然放弃一切，甚至连一句像样的道别都没有就离开了。

5
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:47.000
The letters were written in Beverly's handwriting from a notepad she kept in her home. Both were postmarked Wednesday, July 18 and were sent from the city of Miami, about 37 miles south of Pompano Beach. When calls to Beverly's home phone failed to connect, Jane visited a police station to report her missing. There was little they could do, as the letters indicated that Beverly had left of her own accord. That night, Steve and Jane headed to Pompano Beach to investigate the matter for themselves.
信是用贝弗利的笔迹写在家里的一本记事本上的。两封信的邮戳都是7月18日星期三，从距离庞帕诺比奇以南约37英里的迈阿密市寄出。在拨打贝弗利家里的电话无人接听后，简前往警察局报案称其失踪。警方对此无能为力，因为信件表明贝弗利是自愿离开的。那天晚上，史蒂夫和简前往庞帕诺比奇亲自调查此事。

6
00:03:47.000 --> 00:04:33.000
They arrived at Beverly's home, an upper-level apartment in a two-story condominium building. It was one of many similarly designed complexes that lined South Flagler Avenue. The long, quiet street was situated on the cusp of a dense neighborhood. Beverly's condo was compact. It featured two bedrooms and a balcony that overlooked the residence car park. Upon arrival, Steve and Jane noticed Beverly's red Volkswagen Fox wasn't in its usual parking spot. She wasn't home, but it didn't appear as though she had packed up and left for good.
他们来到了贝弗利家，这是一栋两层共管公寓楼的上层公寓。它是南弗拉格勒大道旁众多设计相似的住宅区之一。这条长而安静的街道位于一个密集居民区的边缘。贝弗利的公寓很紧凑。它有两间卧室和一个俯瞰住宅停车场的阳台。到达后，史蒂夫和简发现贝弗利的红色大众福克斯汽车并不在它通常的停车位上。她不在家，但看起来并不像是已经收拾好行李永久离开的样子。

7
00:04:33.000 --> 00:05:19.000
There were dirty dishes in the kitchen sink, a nightgown had been left on her unmade bed, clothes were in the closet and strewn on the floor. Although there were also signs indicating that Beverly had no intention of returning, the telephone had been disconnected, the answering machine kept alongside it was gone, and there was no trace of Beverly's two pet cats. Steve and Jane rummaged through some drawers and discovered Beverly's address book, passport, and birth certificate were also missing. Steve contacted Beverly's employer at Glendale Federal Bank to see whether they could shed
厨房水槽里有脏盘子，未整理的床上留有一件睡袍，衣柜里和地板上散落着衣服。尽管也有迹象表明贝弗利无意返回：家里的座机电话已被拔掉，与之放在一起的答录机不见了，而且贝弗利养的两只宠物猫也踪迹全无。史蒂夫和简翻找了一些抽屉，发现贝弗利的通讯录、护照和出生证明也都不见了。史蒂夫联系了贝弗利在格伦代尔联邦银行的雇主，看看他们能否提供

8
00:05:19.000 --> 00:06:03.000
any light on the situation. Beverly worked Monday to Friday in the bank's loans department, but also had a second part-time job at Goodwill, a non-profit organization. Steve was told that Beverly called in sick on Wednesday, July 18, the day before he received her goodbye letter. This was unusual, given Beverly's reputation as a responsible and reliable employee. During the call, she had also asked to speak to someone in the bank's mortgage department. After she was transferred through, Beverly said she no longer wanted her condo and requested
任何关于现状的线索。贝弗利周一到周五在银行的贷款部门工作，但同时还在非营利组织“好市好”（Goodwill）做第二份兼职。史蒂夫被告知，贝弗利在7月18日星期三请了病假，也就是他收到她告别信的前一天。鉴于贝弗利一向是个负责任且可靠的员工，这很不寻常。在通话期间，她还要求与银行抵押贷款部门的人通话。转接后，贝弗利说她不再想要她的公寓，并要求

9
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:40.000
to foreclose on it. She was told that she would have to send a telegram to verify her request. A telegram was subsequently received. It also gave the bank permission to dispose of the personal belongings left in her home. Although the circumstances were strange, Steve began to believe that his sister had just left without a proper explanation. He lodged a missing persons report with the local authorities and also had Beverly's credit cards cancelled.
对其实施止赎。她被告知必须发送一封电报来确认她的请求。随后银行收到了一封电报。电报还授权银行处理她家中留下的个人物品。尽管情况诡异，史蒂夫还是开始相信他的妹妹只是没有留下合理的解释就离开了。他在当地警局报了人口失踪，并挂失了贝弗利的信用卡。

10
00:06:40.000 --> 00:07:27.000
He hoped that cancelling the cards would hinder her travel plans and make her angry enough to reach out to her family. On the evening of Thursday, July 19, 31-year-old Jesse Moorhead and his niece went out to catch bait for bass fishing. They arrived at a wide irrigation canal located 100 miles north of Pompano Beach in a remote area of St. Lucie County. The canal is reached via a dirt track and is bordered by an unkempt grassy embankment. One side of the waterway empties out into the St. Lucie River estuary.
他希望挂失信用卡能阻碍她的旅行计划，并让她气得主动与家人联系。7月19日星期星期四晚上，31岁的杰西·穆尔黑德（Jesse Moorhead）和他的侄女外出捕捉用于垂钓鲈鱼的鱼饵。他们来到了位于庞帕诺比奇以北100英里的圣露西亚县偏远地区的一条宽阔灌溉运河旁。这条运河通过一条泥路到达，周围环绕着无人修剪的草堤。水路的另一端汇入圣露西亚河口。

11
00:07:27.000 --> 00:08:06.000
The other leads south to the state's sprawling tropical wetlands, the Florida River Glades. Just after 7pm, Jesse was walking alongside the canal while his niece waited nearby in his car. On the embankment, he spotted what appeared to be a bag of rags and went over to inspect them. Upon realizing what he had actually discovered, Jesse raced back to his car and contacted the police. Investigators from St. Lucie County Sheriff's Department arrived at the canal and headed
另一端向南通往该州广阔的热带湿地——佛罗里达大沼泽地。刚过晚上7点，杰西沿着运河散步，他的侄女则在附近的汽车里等候。在路堤上，他发现了一个看起来像是一包破布的东西，于是走过去查看。意识到自己究竟发现了什么后，杰西飞奔回车里并报警。圣露西亚县警长办公室的调查人员赶到运河并前往

12
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:45.000
to the location described by Jesse. There, they found the mutilated remains of a female adult. She was dressed in jeans, a single white sandal and a pink floral shirt that was bunched up around her neck. She had been killed elsewhere before her body was dumped at the site. There was a gaping wound on her abdomen, though its cause was unclear. It could have been a deliberate injury or the result of post-mortem trauma to the body, as alligators populated the canal.
杰西描述的地点。在那里，他们发现了女性成人的残缺遗体。她穿着牛仔裤、一只白色凉鞋和一件卷在脖子周围的粉红色碎花衬衫。她在遗体被抛弃到现场之前就在别处被杀害了。她的腹部有一个巨大的伤口，尽管原因尚不清楚。这可能是蓄意伤害，也可能是遗体遭受死后创伤的结果，因为运河里栖息着短吻鳄。

13
00:08:45.000 --> 00:09:26.000
The killer had gone to disturbing lengths to prevent the victim from being identified. Her hands had been removed and she had been crudely decapitated. The missing body parts were not found at the site. Despite this, a pivotal clue had seemingly gone unnoticed by the perpetrator. On the victim's right ankle, hidden under the cuff of her jeans, was a small tattoo of a yellow rose. A description of the tattoo was released to the local media and featured in news reports on the crime.
凶手费尽心机防止死者身份被识别。她的双手被砍掉，并被粗暴地斩首。失踪的身体部位在现场没有找到。尽管如此，凶手似乎还是遗漏了一个关键线索。死者的右脚踝上，藏在牛仔裤裤脚下方，有一个黄玫瑰的小纹身。该纹身的描述被发布给当地媒体，并在有关这起犯罪的新闻报道中播出。

14
00:09:26.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Steve McGowan was at home when his telephone rang at around 10pm. On the other line was a friend of his missing sister, Beverly. She'd just heard the news of the woman's body found in St. Lucie County. The victim had a tattoo of a yellow rose on her right ankle, just like Beverly. The following day, Steve and Jane drove to St. Lucie County to speak with investigators. They provided a photograph of Beverly's rose tattoo, but declined to view the mutilated body as they found the prospect too distressing. The pair were nevertheless certain the woman was their sister.
大约晚上10点，史蒂夫·麦高恩正在家中，这时他的电话铃响了。电话那头是失踪妹妹贝弗利的一位朋友。她刚听到在圣露西亚县发现一具女尸的消息。死者的右脚踝上有一个黄玫瑰纹身，和贝弗利的一模一样。第二天，史蒂夫和简开车前往圣露西亚县与调查人员交谈。他们提供了一张贝弗利玫瑰纹身的照片，但拒绝查看残缺的尸体，因为他们觉得这个前景太令人痛心了。尽管如此，两人确信这个女人就是他们的妹妹。

15
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:59.000
They told investigators that Beverly had another tattoo just above her waistline of a rabbit from the animated Disney film, Bambi. This tattoo's location matched the victim's abdomen wound. It appeared as though the perpetrator had cut out the rabbit tattoo to hinder the identification process, but had missed the rose tattoo. The decapitation was also imperfect, as a portion of the victim's lower jaw still remained. A dental expert compared a tooth and filling from the remains to Beverly McGowan's dental records.
他们告诉调查人员，贝弗利在腰线上方还有另一个纹身，图案是迪斯尼动画电影《小鹿斑比》中的一只兔子。这个纹身的位置与受害者的腹部伤口相吻合。看起来凶手是为了阻碍辨认过程而切除了兔子纹身，却漏掉了玫瑰纹身。斩首也不完全彻底，因为受害者下巴的一部分仍然保留着。一名牙科专家将残骸中的一颗牙齿和补牙材料与贝弗利·麦高恩的牙科记录进行了比对。

16
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:44.000
Four days after Beverly's siblings received her goodbye letters, she was officially identified as the woman found by the St. Lucie County Irrigation Canal. A medical examiner struggled to establish a cause of death due to the severe mutilation. Beverly's abdomen tattoo had likely been cut out with a knife, while a chainsaw was used to remove her hands and head. It appeared as though her throat had been cut, but it couldn't be ruled with absolute certainty that this was what killed her. There was also a possibility that she had been bludgeoned or shot in the head.
在贝弗利的兄弟姐妹收到她的告别信四天后，她被正式确认为圣露西亚县灌溉运河边发现的女性。由于遗体残缺严重，法医很难确定死因。贝弗利的腹部纹身可能是用刀割掉的，而链锯则被用来切除她的双手和头部。看起来她的喉咙被割过，但无法绝对断定这就是致死原因。她也有可能被钝器殴打或头部中枪。

17
00:11:44.000 --> 00:12:29.000
There was no evidence of sexual assault. The last time Beverly was seen alive was at work on Tuesday, July 17. She hadn't mentioned anything to colleagues about going away on a trip. That evening, she phoned a friend for a chat they had every Tuesday. The next day, her employers received the call from someone they believed to be Beverly, stating that she was unwell and wouldn't be coming in. An examination of Beverly's condo failed to uncover blood or any suspicious fingerprints, fibres, or hairs.
没有性侵的证据。贝弗利最后一次被看到活著是在7月17日星期二的工作中。她没有向同事提及任何要外出旅行的事。那天晚上，她给一个朋友打电话聊天，这是她们每周二都有的习惯。第二天，她的雇主接到一个他们认为是贝弗利的人打来的电话，称她身体不舒服，不会来上班了。对贝弗利公寓的检查没有发现血迹或任何可疑的指纹、纤维或毛发。

18
00:12:29.000 --> 00:13:20.000
There was no sign of a struggle having taken place. The farewell letters to her family were puzzling, as they were in Beverly's handwriting. There was no sign that they had been coerced, yet they ended with the words goodbye, Bev. Her siblings said that Beverly would typically sign off letters by simply writing her name. They had no explanation as to who would harm Beverly or why. She was quiet, independent, and mostly kept to herself. She loved and doted on her nephews and they depended on her. She wasn't wealthy and she didn't have any problematic relationships.
没有发生过打斗的迹象。给她家人的告别信令人费解，因为它们是贝弗利的笔迹。没有迹象表明它们是被强迫写下的，然而信的结尾却是“再见，贝夫（Goodbye, Bev）”。她的兄弟姐妹说，贝弗利通常只会简单地签上自己的名字来结束信件。他们无法解释谁会伤害贝弗利，也不知道为什么。她安静、独立，大部分时间都独来独往。她爱她的侄子们并对他们百般呵护，而侄子们也依赖她。她并不富有，也没有任何有问题的恋爱关系。

19
00:13:20.000 --> 00:14:02.000
Beverly's life had been marred by tragedy. Her first two boyfriends were killed in separate car accidents. She started dating again to move on, but would end relationships when they became serious. Steve later heard rumours of his sister exploring her sexuality during her early 30s. He described her as someone who travelled to the beat of a different drummer and believed she was only ever looking for love. Despite her traumatic past, Steve was clear that Beverly had recently been at her most content.
贝弗利的生活饱受悲剧摧残。她的前两个男友都在不同的车祸中丧生。为了走出阴影，她开始重新约会，但当关系变得严肃时，她总是会结束这段关系。史蒂夫后来听到传言说，他的妹妹在30岁出头时曾探索过自己的性取向。他形容她是一个特立独行的人，并相信她所寻求的始终只有爱。尽管有着痛苦的过去，但史蒂夫明确表示，贝弗利最近一段时间是她最满足的时候。

20
00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:43.000
He did report one concerning incident. A week before Beverly disappeared, she told Steve about an unsettling message left on her answering machine. She didn't recognise the male caller's voice. She was recorded saying, I know where you live and I can't wait for us to be together. Troubled by the message, Beverly took her answering machine into work and played it to her colleagues. Curiously, the machine was missing from Beverly's abandoned condo.
他的确报告了一起令人担忧的事件。在贝弗利失踪前一周，她告诉史蒂夫答录机上留下一条令人不安的信息。她听不出这个男声是谁。录音里说：“我知道你住在哪里，我迫不及待地想让我们在一起。”被这条信息困扰的贝弗利把答录机带到单位放给同事听。奇怪的是，这个机器在贝弗利被遗弃的公寓里不见了。

21
00:14:43.000 --> 00:15:27.000
Beverly valued her privacy, but working two jobs wasn't enough to pay off her mortgage. To supplement her income, she'd rented out her spare bedroom on two previous occasions. Neither roommate worked out in the long run. The first, a woman named Brenda, had clashed with Beverly over lifestyle differences. She was replaced by a man named George. She liked George, but he left after several months to get his own place. Both Brenda and George were questioned in relation to Beverly's murder, but were ruled out as suspects.
贝弗利很重视自己的隐私，但打两份工还不足以还清房贷。为了增加收入，她曾在前两次将多余的卧室出租。从长远来看，这两位室友都不合适。第一个室友是一个名叫布伦达（Brenda）的女人，她因生活方式的不同而与贝弗利产生冲突。她后来被一个叫乔治（George）的男人取代。她挺喜欢乔治，但他几个月后就搬出去找自己的地方了。布伦达和乔治都曾就贝弗利的谋杀案接受盘问，但都被排除在嫌疑人之外。

22
00:15:27.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Investigators also spoke with a painter named Mike who lived in Beverly's apartment complex. The pair had struck up a close friendship and caught up for dinner several nights a week. Mike was adamant that he would never harm Beverly. He said he was out of town at the time of the murder, preparing for a gallery exhibition. His alibi checked out, and Mike too was ruled out. He said he had spoken to Beverly two days before she disappeared. Mike called to ask if she wanted to have dinner with him that night. Beverly typically accepted spontaneous plans, but not on this occasion.
调查人员还与一名住在贝弗利公寓大楼里名叫迈克（Mike）的油漆工交谈。两人建立了亲密的友谊，每周有几个晚上聚在一起吃晚餐。迈克坚称他绝不会伤害贝弗利。他说谋杀发生时他不在镇上，正在为画廊展览做准备。他的不在场证明得到了核实，迈克也被排除嫌疑。他说他在贝弗利失踪前两天和她说过话。迈克打电话问她那天晚上愿不愿意和他一起吃晚餐。贝弗利通常会接受突如其来的计划，但这次没有。

23
00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:58.000
She rejected Mike's offer, explaining that she was going to spend a time with a potential new roommate named Dallas. In early July, Beverly told several acquaintances that she'd placed an advertisement for a new roommate in the Fort Lauderdale Sun Sentinel newspaper. Applications came through, and Beverly interviewed several candidates in the week prior to her murder. When searching her home, investigators found a notepad with a list of applicants' details. Each entry featured a full name, a phone number, and an appointment time to view the condo.
她拒绝了迈克的邀请，解释说她要和一位潜在的新室友达拉斯（Dallas）共度时光。在7月初，贝弗利告诉几位熟人，她在《劳德代尔堡太阳哨兵报》上登广告招租新室友。申请接踵而至，贝弗利在谋杀案发生前的一周面试了几个候选人。在搜查她的家时，调查人员发现了一个记事本，上面列有申请人的详细信息。每个条目都包含全名、电话号码以及查看公寓的预约时间。

24
00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:37.000
